@startuml
' REVIEWED_MAIN_2026_05_13: aligned to current merged code; large-investment retained pending simplification merge.
title WYSIWYS for Corda Protocol V1 — Tier 2 BAU Operations (Out-of-Band Verification)
skinparam maxMessageSize 250
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
autonumber

box "Environment A (Dirty / Untrusted)" #LightPink
actor "Vault Manager\n(Initiator)" as Manager
participant "Protocol UI / dApp\n(Untrusted)" as UI
end box

box "Communication" #White
participant "Slack/PagerDuty\n(OOB Channel)" as OOB
end box

box "Environment B (Secure / Zero-Trust)" #LightGreen
actor "Tier 2 Signer\n(Approver)" as Approver
participant "Security App\n(Untrusted Transport)" as App
participant "Advanced HW Wallet\n(Clear Signing)" as HW
end box

box "Infrastructure (Tech Specific)" #LightBlue
participant "Private RPC\n(e.g., Helius)" as RPC
participant "Simulation API\n(Blowfish/Blocksec)" as Sim
database "Solana Mainnet\n(Squads V4)" as Squads
end box

== Phase 1: On-Chain Proposal Creation ==
Manager -> UI: Drafts BAU Action\n(e.g., Transfer 50k USDC / Update Config)
UI -> Squads: Send `CreateProposal` & `AddInstruction`
Squads --> UI: Proposal PDA Created (e.g., Index 88)

== Phase 2: Out-of-Band Hand-off ==
Manager -> OOB: "Tier 2 Action: Please review Proposal #88.\nIntent: Transfer 50k USDC to Yield Vault."
OOB -> Approver: Receives secure notification

== Phase 3: Cryptographic Fetch (Zero-Trust) ==
Approver -> App: Inputs Proposal Index "88"
App -> RPC: Fetch account data for Proposal PDA (Index 88)
note right of App: Bypasses the Web UI entirely.\nFetches cryptographic truth directly.
RPC --> App: Returns raw, serialized instruction bytes

== Phase 4: Intent Simulation (WYSIWYS Translation) ==
App -> Sim: Send raw payload for transaction simulation
Sim --> App: Returns Decoded State Changes\n(e.g., "-50,000 USDC", "+50,000 yUSDC")
App -> HW: Pass raw instruction payload to Hardware Wallet

== Phase 5: Hardware-Level Clear Signing & Verification ==
note over HW: **FIRMWARE DECODING**\nHW natively parses the payload or \nverifies the simulation data on its own chip.
HW -> Approver: Screen displays:\n**"Action: Transfer 50,000 USDC"**\n**"To: Yield Vault Address"**
note over Approver: **THE MANUAL CHECK**\nApprover manually verifies the Hardware screen\nexactly matches the Intent stated in Slack.\n(Ensures UI didn't inject a drain payload).

== Phase 6: Air-Gapped Signature ==
Approver -> HW: Confirms text matches intent (Presses Sign)
HW --> App: Returns Cryptographic Signature

== Phase 7: Broadcast & Squads V4 Timelock ==
App -> RPC: Broadcast Signed `Approve` TX
RPC -> Squads: Execute `ApproveTransaction`
Squads --> App: State: Proposal Approved (Signer added)

note over Squads: **Tier 2 Protocol Logic:**\nIf Approvals reach Threshold (e.g., 2 of 5):\nStatus = 'Approved'\n`approved_at` timestamp recorded.\n**Tier 2 Timelock (e.g., 24h) begins.**

App -> Approver: "Success. 2/5 Reached. 24h Timelock Active."

@enduml